# Active Count — LOCKED baseline (P8.19.8)

Active Inventory Count keyboard / scroll / runway behavior is an **approved production baseline**. Do not change it unless a sprint **explicitly** authorizes modifying this contract.

Baseline reference: P8.19.8 (post P8.19.9 rollback). Permanent until a newer approved baseline replaces it.

## Protected (must not change)

- Keyboard behavior and VisualViewport handling
- Scroll ownership; **320px** bottom runway (`--inventory-count-sheet-end-runway`)
- Frozen table header; footer position / visibility above keyboard
- Previous / Next / Complete Location positioning
- Active input auto-reveal; Enter → Save → Next
- Body height chain; iPad landscape layout; desktop mirror

## Before any Inventory Count CSS / layout edit

Inspect whether the change touches selectors that participate in:

`keyboard` · `visualViewport` · `overflow` · `height` · `min-height` · `max-height` · `flex` · `grid` · `grid-template` · `sticky` · `bottom` · `inset` · viewport calculations

**If yes → STOP.** Report why. Do not implement unless the sprint explicitly authorizes locked-baseline changes.

## Allowed without baseline authorization

Typography, spacing, colors, borders, shadows, icons, copy, button styling, information hierarchy — **only if** they do **not** alter layout flow, grid/flex contracts, viewport math, keyboard, scrolling, footer geometry, or runway.

## Mandatory end-of-sprint regression checklist

- Keyboard opens correctly; footer remains visible
- Scroll owner unchanged; 320px runway preserved
- Frozen header preserved; Enter → Save → Next works
- Final rows reachable; no page scroll; no layout jump
- iPad landscape identical to locked baseline

**If any regress → STOP.** Rollback the sprint. Do not “repair” in the same sprint. Restore the locked baseline first; only then start a new isolated sprint.
